rk, via `recovery::highest_tree_identifier_watermark_in_the_ring`) gives the same watermark for the row-writing publish, covered by the watermark term taken from the records; `roll_back_by_a_forward_publish` (administrator rollback computing the tree ID and inode number watermarks, via `recovery::readable_roots`, the place ② of C584 (before writing the system configuration and for rollback watermarks, unreadable slots are still taken as no root)) gives the same two watermarks for the rollback publish, since both are maxed with the term of the current version and, in single-fault states that can be reached, the ring term is not above the current version's. What would overturn this: for the first two, a reachable state where the root with the highest txg (or highest watermark) reads bad while no record with a txg (or watermark) not below it can be read; for the third, a reachable single-fault state where a root in the ring has a tree ID watermark above the current version's, or a root not abandoned by the current instance table has an inode number watermark above the current version's. The fourth, `newest_root_from_the_version_the_system_configuration_witnessed_up_to_the_chosen_root_to_fall_back_to` in `crates/singlefs-core/src/recovery.rs` (candidate of the F2 fall-back, via `readable_roots`), has a consequence: when the root slot of the fall-back target goes bad once in the two reads that judge candidates, recovery, read-only mount and writable mount change from "fall back to that version and succeed" to "report the selected version as unreadable / refuse"; this is an availability consequence, never a wrong version or a wrong number (the check that refuses a fall-back which would skip a publish whose last record is readable but whose root is not turns it into a refusal; with that check switched off the same bad read silently lands all three on an older version). Ruling (user popup, "甲：读坏的槽一律重读一次（推荐）"): when the F2 candidate judgement reads the root ring, every bad slot is reread once; a reread that yields a self-verified root is used as read, and a reread that is still bad lands on that refusal; the clause goes into the "root slot reads bad this time" row of D16 (Publish Semantics) settled item 1. The test cases are in `crates/singlefs-harness/tests/fall_back_candidate_root_slot_reading_bad_once_does_not_change_where_recovery_and_both_mounts_land.rs` (two, one for a read that fails once and one for a self-verification that fails once; both red on today's code) | The fix awaits the next crates batch: the read in `crates/singlefs-core/src/recovery.rs` becomes a per-slot reread once on a bad read (fix 甲 in section six of the investigation report); the mutation row is written once the fix has settled, and `.claude/gate.d/crates-mutation-light-rows.tsv` needs a row for the new target | Clause settled (user popup of 2026-10-22); reach narrowed to the fourth caller (investigation of 2026-10-22); destination: milestone 3 II·5 (triage 2026-10-19; on 2026-10-20 the main agent decided not to close the entry and narrowed its reach to these four; on 2026-10-22 narrowed again to the fourth). | 2026-09-26 root-cause report of implementation round 4 C, section 5 question 1 |
